---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Constitution of India Privacy Policy - Logicpath Systems">
    <section class="legal-page" style="padding-top: 120px; min-height: 100vh;">
        <div class="container reveal">
            <div class="glass-card" style="padding: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem);">
                <header style="margin-bottom: 3rem; text-align: center;">
                    <h1 class="gradient-text">Privacy Policy</h1>
                    <p style="color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;"><strong>Constitution of India</strong></p>
                    <p style="color: var(--text-secondary);">Logicpath Systems &middot; <strong>Last updated:</strong> 27 November 2026 &middot; <strong>Effective from:</strong> 27 November 2026</p>
                </header>

                <main class="legal-content">
                    <p>This Privacy Policy explains how Logicpath Systems (&ldquo;we&rdquo;, &ldquo;us&rdquo;) handles information in the Constitution of India app for Android (the &ldquo;App&rdquo;). The App is free.</p>
                    <p>By using the App, you agree to this policy. If you do not agree, please do not use the App.</p>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>1. Summary</h2>
                    <ul>
                        <li>You can read, learn and practise without creating an account. We never ask for your email address or phone number.</li>
                        <li>Most of what you do stays on your phone: your progress, bookmarks, quiz history, profile name and photo.</li>
                        <li>Live Battle (playing with friends) sends a small amount of game data to our server. This is your player name, a random guest ID, and your answers and score.</li>
                        <li>We use Google AdMob for ads, Firebase Analytics for usage statistics and Firebase Cloud Messaging for notifications. These Google services collect some device information.</li>
                        <li>We do not sell your personal information.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>2. Information stored only on your phone</h2>
                    <p>The App saves the following on your device. We do not receive it.</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Reading progress, bookmarks and saved articles</li>
                        <li>Quiz, mock test and Daily Challenge results, XP, streaks and achievements</li>
                        <li>Your profile name, and a profile photo if you choose one from your gallery</li>
                        <li>Your Live Battle history and match reports (&ldquo;My battles&rdquo;)</li>
                        <li>App settings, such as theme and notification preferences</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>If your phone backs up app data, Android's own backup may include this information (for example, to your Google account). Your Live Battle login is excluded from backups.</p>
                    <p>Uninstalling the App, or clearing its data in Android settings, deletes this information from your phone.</p>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>3. Live Battle</h2>
                    <p>Live Battle lets you play a timed quiz with friends using a room code or a QR code.</p>

                    <h3>What we collect</h3>
                    <p>When you host or join a battle, the App signs you in as an anonymous guest and sends the following to our server:</p>
                    <div class="table-wrapper">
                        <table>
                            <thead>
                                <tr>
                                    <th>Information</th>
                                    <th>Why</th>
                                </tr>
                            </thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>A random guest ID, created by the App. It is not linked to your name, email, phone number or Google account.</td>
                                    <td>To recognise you in a battle and stop cheating</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>Your player name: a random name such as &ldquo;Noble Swan&rdquo;, or one you type, up to 15 characters</td>
                                    <td>To show you to the other players</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>The battle code, the questions you received, your answers, your score and the time you took</td>
                                    <td>To run the game and work out the ranking</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>When you joined, started and finished, and whether you were the host or were removed by the host</td>
                                    <td>To run the game</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>Reports that you, or another player, sent about an offensive player name</td>
                                    <td>To replace offensive names and prevent abuse</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>A record of how often you create or join battles</td>
                                    <td>To stop spam. It is deleted after 1 day.</td>
                                </tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>

                    <h3>Who can see it</h3>
                    <p>The other players in the same battle can see your player name, score, position and time. The answer review shows each player only their own answers.</p>

                    <h3>Where it is stored</h3>
                    <p>Battle data is stored with Supabase, our database provider, on servers in Tokyo, Japan. Supabase may keep technical logs, such as IP addresses and request times, to keep its service secure and reliable. See the <a href="https://supabase.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);">Supabase Privacy Policy</a>.</p>

                    <h3>How long we keep it</h3>
                    <p>Battles and everything in them are deleted from our server 30 days after the battle was created. Your match reports in &ldquo;My battles&rdquo; stay on your phone until you delete them.</p>

                    <h3>Deleting your battle data</h3>
                    <p>Go to Settings &rarr; Delete Battle Data in the App. This:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>removes your name from past battles on our server, where you then appear as &ldquo;Former player&rdquo;,</li>
                        <li>unlinks your scores and answers from your guest ID, so they can no longer be connected to you, and</li>
                        <li>deletes your other records, such as join and spam-check records, and</li>
                        <li>clears &ldquo;My battles&rdquo; on your phone.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <h3>Older versions</h3>
                    <p>Older versions of the App ran Live Battle on Google Firebase, and stored player names, scores and battle results there. If you used an older version and want that data removed, contact us (see section 13).</p>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>4. Camera</h2>
                    <p>The App asks for camera access only when you tap Scan QR code to join a battle. The camera image is processed on your phone to read the code. It is not saved, and it is not sent to us or to anyone else.</p>
                    <p>You can refuse camera access and still join a battle by typing the code.</p>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>5. Photos</h2>
                    <p>If you choose a profile photo, the App reads that one picture from your gallery and keeps a small copy on your phone. It is not uploaded.</p>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>6. Notifications</h2>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Daily reminders and study tips are scheduled on your phone.</li>
                        <li>Daily article notifications are sent through Firebase Cloud Messaging (Google). To deliver them, Firebase uses a device token that identifies the App on your phone.</li>
                        <li>You can turn notifications off at any time in Android settings.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>7. Advertising (Google AdMob)</h2>
                    <p>The App shows ads from Google AdMob: banners, full-screen ads at natural breaks, and optional rewarded ads.</p>
                    <p>To show and measure ads, Google may collect:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>your device's advertising ID,</li>
                        <li>your IP address and approximate location derived from it,</li>
                        <li>device and app information, and</li>
                        <li>how you interact with ads.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>Ads may be personalised based on this information. You can reset or delete your advertising ID, or turn off personalised ads, in Android Settings &rarr; Google &rarr; Ads (the wording varies by phone).</p>
                    <p>See <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);">how Google uses information from apps that use its services</a> and the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);">Google Privacy Policy</a>.</p>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>8. Analytics (Google Analytics for Firebase)</h2>
                    <p>We use Google Analytics for Firebase to learn which features are used and to improve the App. It collects:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>app usage events, such as screens opened, quizzes started and battles played,</li>
                        <li>an app instance ID,</li>
                        <li>device model, operating system version and app version, and</li>
                        <li>approximate location (country or city).</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>We do not send your name, your battle answers or the content you read to Analytics.</p>
                    <p>See <a href="https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);">Firebase Analytics data use</a>.</p>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>9. Other Google services</h2>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Google Play Services support Firebase, ads and app updates.</li>
                        <li>Google Play In-App Review may ask you to rate the App. Your rating goes to Google Play, not to us.</li>
                        <li>If the App crashes, Google Play may collect crash reports and device information for us, in line with your phone's settings.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>10. Sharing and links</h2>
                    <ul>
                        <li>When you share your progress, a battle code or an invite link, the App opens your phone's share menu. You choose which app it goes to. We do not see what you share.</li>
                        <li>Invite links open our web page at <a href="https://constitution-2026.web.app" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);">constitution-2026.web.app</a>, which only shows the battle code and links to the App.</li>
                        <li>The App links to other apps on Google Play and to external websites. Their own privacy policies apply.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>We share information only:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>with the service providers named in this policy, so the App can work;</li>
                        <li>when required by law; or</li>
                        <li>to protect the safety of our users or the App.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>We do not sell your personal information.</p>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>11. Security</h2>
                    <p>We protect your information with reasonable measures:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>All data is sent over encrypted connections (HTTPS).</li>
                        <li>Battle data can only be read and changed through checked server functions. Players cannot read the database directly.</li>
                        <li>The correct answers stay on the server until a battle ends.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>No method of transmission or storage is 100% secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security.</p>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>12. Children</h2>
                    <p>The App is an educational app for a general audience. It is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from them.</p>
                    <p>Live Battle does not ask for real names. Players can choose a random name, and offensive names can be reported and are replaced.</p>
                    <p>If you believe a child under 13 has given us personal information, contact us and we will delete it.</p>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>13. Your choices and rights</h2>
                    <p>Depending on where you live, including under India's Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023, you may have the right to:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>ask what personal information we hold about you,</li>
                        <li>correct or delete it,</li>
                        <li>withdraw consent, and</li>
                        <li>raise a complaint.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>To do this:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>use Settings &rarr; Delete Battle Data in the App, or</li>
                        <li>email us at <a href="mailto:contact@logicpathsystems.com" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);"><strong>contact@logicpathsystems.com</strong></a>.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>Battle data is linked only to a random guest ID. Please send your request from the same phone, or include a battle code you played, so we can find your data.</p>
                    <p>For data held by Google (ads, analytics, notifications), you can also use Google's own controls.</p>
                    <p><strong>Grievance contact:</strong> <a href="mailto:contact@logicpathsystems.com" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);"><strong>contact@logicpathsystems.com</strong></a>. We aim to reply within 30 days.</p>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>14. International transfers</h2>
                    <p>Our service providers may process information outside India: Supabase in Japan, and Google in various countries. They protect it under their own privacy and security commitments.</p>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>15. Changes to this policy</h2>
                    <p>We may update this policy from time to time. We will post the new version on this page and change the &ldquo;Last updated&rdquo; date. Significant changes may also be shown in the App.</p>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>16. Contact us</h2>
                    <p><strong>Logicpath Systems</strong><br/>
                    Email: <a href="mailto:contact@logicpathsystems.com" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);"><strong>contact@logicpathsystems.com</strong></a></p>
                </main>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
</Layout>

<style>
    .legal-content h2 {
        color: var(--text-primary);
        margin-top: 2.5rem;
        margin-bottom: 1rem;
        font-size: 1.5rem;
    }

    .legal-content h3 {
        color: var(--text-primary);
        margin-top: 1.5rem;
        margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
        font-size: 1.25rem;
    }

    .legal-content p, .legal-content ul {
        color: var(--text-secondary);
        margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
        font-size: 1.05rem;
        line-height: 1.7;
    }

    .legal-content ul {
        padding-left: 2rem;
        margin-bottom: 2rem;
    }

    .legal-content li {
        margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    }

    .table-wrapper {
        overflow-x: auto;
        margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    }

    .legal-content table {
        width: 100%;
        border-collapse: collapse;
        margin-bottom: 1rem;
    }

    .legal-content th,
    .legal-content td {
        padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
        text-align: left;
        border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
        color: var(--text-secondary);
        font-size: 1.05rem;
        line-height: 1.6;
    }

    .legal-content th {
        color: var(--text-primary);
        font-weight: 600;
    }
</style>
